    "name": "When Does Garage Insulation Require an Inspection?",
    "text": "When Does Garage Insulation Require an Inspection?",
    "answerCount": 1,
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "It’s a common question: when do you actually need an inspection for garage insulation? While simply adding insulation to an existing, unconditioned garage might not always trigger an inspection, there are definitely key scenarios where it's a must. The biggest one is when you're converting a garage into habitable living space. If your garage is going to become a bedroom, office, or any other conditioned area, then insulation, air sealing, and overall energy performance will definitely need to satisfy local code and inspection standards. This means your R-value and proper installation will be scrutinized. Another time an inspection is usually required is when the work involves a permit. If you're doing a larger renovation that already requires a building permit, the insulation phase often falls under that same inspection umbrella. Inspectors typically verify things like coverage, thickness, and proper vapor barrier placement to ensure everything aligns with local energy codes. The general rule of thumb is that work cannot be concealed until all required inspections (including framing and rough electrical/plumbing) are passed, and insulation is usually one of those steps. So, if you're planning a major garage overhaul or conversion in areas like Lone Tree or Castle Rock, don't skip this critical step. HH Remodeling LLC can help you understand the specific requirements for your project and ensure everything is up to code before any drywall goes up.",
      "author": {
        "@type": "Organization",
        "name": "HH Remodeling LLC"
      }
    }
  },
